.SH ENVIRONMENT
\f[B]BWM_LOG_LEVEL\f[R] Log level for \f[I]\(ti/.cache/bwm.log\f[R].
One of \f[I]critical\f[R], \f[I]error\f[R], \f[I]warning\f[R],
\f[I]info\f[R] or \f[I]debug\f[R]; an unrecognized value falls back to
the default and says so in the log.
Default \f[I]warning\f[R]; set to \f[I]debug\f[R] to record each
vault\(cqs status check, unlock and entry load.
A backgrounded daemon sends its output to /dev/null, so this and
\f[B]\(enforeground\f[R] are how to see what it is doing.
.PP
The log records vault entry names, item ids and server URLs, but never
passwords, TOTP seeds, session tokens or vault contents.
It is created mode 0600.
.PP
\f[B]DISPLAY\f[R], \f[B]WAYLAND_DISPLAY\f[R] When neither is set, bwm
prompts on the terminal instead of through a launcher, which is what
makes the initial login, 2FA included, work on a headless machine.
